    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0320" n="1154" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/387b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7103. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 279. Repeat to Schmedeman:</p>
                <p>The following memorandum represents the present status of our negotiations with
                    Doctor Nansen. It
                    contains some matters still under discussion but Doctor Nansen believes that if it is
                    given to his Government in order that they may cable him their comments time
                    will be saved in reaching a final conclusion.</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of the draft agreement.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d276-f1"/>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d276-f1" n="1" xml:id="d276-f1-content">
                <p>Generally identical with the final text printed, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg1170">p. 1170</ref>, except for certain
                    alterations made in consequence of the Norwegian negotiator’s letter of Apr. 12,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg1155">p. 1155</ref>.
                    Passages of the draft which were radically altered in the final text are printed
                    as footnotes to the pertinent portions of that letter.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
